Since $\rho>0$ is arbitrary, letting $\rho\to0$ gives $\Pr\{\mathcal D_\epsilon\}
 \sim
 C_M
 \epsilon^{\frac{M-1}{2}}.$ Using the small-angle expansion $2\sin^2\left(\frac{x}{2}\right)
