	\centering
	\includegraphics[width=0.4\textwidth]{fig3.pdf}
	\caption{Secrecy rate versus $\tau$ under different parameters.}
	\label{fig3}
\end{figure}
After determining the sensing time fraction $\tau$ and the uncertainty inflation factor $\kappa$, the convergence performance of the proposed AO algorithm is shown in Fig.~\ref{fig4}. As the number of iterations increases, the CRLB decreases while the worst-case secrecy rate increases, and both eventually converge. The sensing optimization converges within a relatively small number of iterations, whereas the secrecy-rate optimization requires more iterations due to the coupling among the beamforming vector, RIS phase shifts, and Eve's location uncertainty. These results demonstrate that the proposed AO algorithm achieves stable convergence within a limited number of iterations.
