As shown in Fig.~\ref{fig6}, the worst-case secrecy rate increases with the BS transmit power for all RIS configurations. Moreover, increasing the number of RIS elements further improves the secrecy performance by providing more reflection and phase-control degrees of freedom for enhancing Bob's signal and suppressing information leakage toward Eve. Compared with random RIS phase shifts, the proposed optimized RIS phase design achieves higher secrecy rates across different RIS sizes and transmit power levels, demonstrating the effectiveness of jointly optimizing the RIS phase shifts and transmit beamforming for robust secure transmission.
