Fig.~\ref{fig7} shows the secrecy rate versus transmit power for different schemes. For all schemes, the secrecy rate increases with transmit power, and the perfect-CSI benchmark achieves the highest secrecy rate since it is not affected by Eve's location uncertainty. In the low-power regime, the advantage of the proposed scheme over the no-RIS and random-RIS schemes is not yet pronounced. As the transmit power increases, the proposed scheme improves more rapidly and gradually outperforms both, indicating that it can better exploit the spatial degrees of freedom at higher transmit power. In the high-power regime, the proposed scheme approaches the perfect-CSI benchmark, demonstrating that the proposed robust optimization can effectively mitigate the performance loss caused by Eve's location uncertainty.
