When the sufficient condition in Theorem~\ref{thm:single_optimal_rotation}
is satisfied, the boundary cases are first identified using
\eqref{eq:optimal_delta_exact}, and bisection is applied when the optimum
lies in the interior.
Otherwise, a one-dimensional search is performed.
\textbf{Closed-form}: the rotation budget is determined by the proposed
second-order closed-form solution in \eqref{eq:delta_cf}.
\textbf{Delay-unaware}: the RA orientations are optimized without
accounting for the mechanical rotation delay, while the actual rotation
time is included when evaluating the effective transmission rate.
\textbf{Fixed Antenna}: all RAs remain at the common reference orientation $\mathbf f_0$.
We first evaluate the closed-form solution derived from the second-order
expansion.
